---
import GuideSection from "../../components/GuideSection.astro";
import Button from "../../components/ui/Button.astro";
---

<GuideSection id="dictation" title="Dictation on your Mac">
  <p>
    Local speech and refinement models process dictation on your Mac. Cloud
    speech providers receive your audio. Cloud refinement providers receive your
    transcript and any context you enable. Your provider keys are stored in the
    macOS Keychain.
  </p>
  <p>
    Website analytics below cover this website only; they never collect data
    from the Airdraft Mac app. The app's own optional usage data is described in
    the next section. The website's interactive samples use authored text and
    never record your microphone.
  </p>
</GuideSection>

<GuideSection id="app-telemetry" title="Optional usage data in the Mac app">
  <p>
    Official Airdraft downloads can send anonymous usage counts and crash
    reports, but only after you choose Share Anonymous Usage Data. The app asks
    once, on its Ready setup step or on Home, and sends nothing before you
    answer. Builds you compile from source never send usage data or crash
    reports.
  </p>
  <p>With your consent, the app sends only these events:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>App launched</strong>: app version and build, macOS major version,
      processor type, interface language and license state (trial, licensed,
      expired or none).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Setup finished</strong>: completed or skipped.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Dictation completed</strong>: speech engine family and whether it
      runs on your Mac or online, refinement provider type, built-in profile or
      "custom", recording length and stop-to-delivery time in ranges, delivery
      status and whether refinement was applied or fell back to your transcript.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Dictation failed</strong>: a category such as permission, missing
      model, missing key, speech error or delivery failure. Cancelled dictations
      are not reported.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Model download finished</strong>: the model's identifier from
      Airdraft's built-in catalogue and whether the download succeeded, failed
      or was cancelled.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Meeting transcribed</strong>: length in ranges and speech engine
      family.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>License event</strong>: trial started or license activated.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Usage data choice</strong>: sent when you turn sharing on, and
      once when you turn it off.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Crash reports</strong>: the error type, stack frames and the
      loaded system and app libraries needed to locate the fault, with user
      names removed from file paths.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Every event also carries the app's tag, macOS and app versions, the PostHog
    library version and a random identifier that is not linked to you. The app
    never sends your words, transcripts, audio, vocabulary, prompts, clipboard,
    the apps you dictate into, window titles, web addresses, file names or
    paths, provider endpoints, API keys, license keys, custom model names, your
    Mac's name or your email address. The app accepts only these fixed events
    and values and discards anything else before sending.
  </p>
  <p>
    Turn sharing off at any time in Settings &gt; Behavior &gt; Share anonymous
    usage data and crash reports. Turning it off stops collection and crash
    capture; unsent events and pending crash reports are removed from your Mac
    the next time Airdraft opens. It does not delete events already received.
  </p>
  <p>
    PostHog processes this data for us in the United States, in the same project
    as the website analytics. The app asks PostHog not to infer your location
    from your IP address, and we configure the project to discard IP addresses;
    the service still receives the network connection. No person profiles are
    created.
  </p>
</GuideSection>

<GuideSection id="website-analytics" title="Optional website analytics">
  <p>
    When website analytics are enabled, we ask before loading PostHog. If you
    allow it, PostHog receives page visits, selected button actions, browser and
    device type, performance measurements, referral domains and campaign labels.
    A random browser identifier connects those events across visits.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not enable session recordings, capture typed text or create identified
    person profiles. We remove URL queries and fragments, referral paths,
    advertising click identifiers and unrecognized event properties before
    sending events. Campaign labels must not contain personal information. We
    configure PostHog to discard IP addresses and disable location enrichment;
    the service still receives the network connection.
  </p>
  <p>
    PostHog uses browser storage after you allow analytics. We also store your
    allow or decline choice on this browser for 180 days. Declining sends no
    website analytics to PostHog. Turning analytics off stops future collection
    and clears the SDK's stored analytics state; it does not delete events
    already received.
  </p>
  <p>
    We honor Global Privacy Control and Do Not Track signals by keeping
    analytics off. Analytics choices apply to this website and browser only.
    JavaScript must be enabled to change the choice or collect analytics.
  </p>
  <p>
    Cloudflare hosts the website and handles network requests and access
    controls separately. Following GitHub or payment links takes you to those
    services, under their own privacy practices.
  </p>
  <p>
    Read <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy">PostHog's privacy notice</a> for
    its service practices.
  </p>
</GuideSection>

<GuideSection id="analytics" title="Your analytics choice">
  <p
    class="analytics-status"
    data-analytics-status
    data-disabled="Website analytics are not enabled on this site."
    data-blocked="Analytics are off because your browser requests no tracking."
    data-allowed="Website analytics are allowed. You can turn them off below."
    data-off="Website analytics are off."
    aria-live="polite"
  >
    Website analytics are off unless you allow them with JavaScript enabled.
  </p>
  <div class="analytics-actions analytics-settings">
    <Button data-analytics-choice="denied">Turn Analytics Off</Button>
    <Button data-analytics-choice="granted">Allow Analytics</Button>
  </div>
</GuideSection>
